Z||000003||Oreif||12-07-2001||08:25 AM||||I installed a set of 4" component speakers in all four spots. They are Polk Audio EX series II.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/speaker1_2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sail_4_1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sail_in_1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Simple Fiero||12-07-2001||01:06 PM||||I have got pioneer 4X10's. I want Rockford 4x6's in the back of mine, they are cheap compared to the infinity's, and they sound ssoooooooo nnniiiicccceeee.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jefrysuko||12-07-2001||04:05 PM||||Here are some options for you.<P>Kenwood KFC-1068S  4" 2-way Speakers Blue pearl-mica IMPP woofer * weather-resistant PEI tweeter * 2-18W RMS power range<P>Regular Price $49.95<BR>Scratch and Dent $39.95<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2000/113/l113KFC1068S.jpeg"> <P><BR>Pioneer TS-A1086 4" 2-way Speakers Durable IMPP woofer * cone tweeter * 2-15W RMS power range<P>Regular Price $69.95<BR>Scratch and Dent $59.46<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/lifestyle/2000/l130TSA1086.jpeg"> <P><BR>Infinity Kappa 42.1i  4" 2-way Speakers Durable green injection-molded quartz poly woofer * rubber surround * ceramic<BR>composite dome tweeter * 2-45W RMS power range * 3-year warranty<P>Regular Price $79.95 <BR>Scratch and Dent $67.96<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2000/108/l108421i.jpeg"> <P><BR>JBL GTO4.2c 4" Component System 4" titanium-composite injection-molded woofers with butyl rubber surrounds * 1/2"<BR>titanium-composite tweeters * in-line crossover modules * frequency response 65-22,000 Hz * power 8-75 watts RMS<P>Regular Price $79.95<BR>Scratch and Dent $67.96<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pix.crutchfield.com/products/2001/109/h109GTO42C-1.jpeg"> <P>All of these products came off the Crutchfield Scratch and Dent page which can be found at <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/S-S7WKioaQ47c/scratchanddent/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/S-S7WKioaQ47c/scratchanddent/</A>  You can fit any of these speakers in the dash with an adapter like Orief made and crutchfield will supply an adapter for the rear.  The last set of speakers will need a hole drilled for the tweeter in the rear.<P>I recently bought two sets of speakers that were scratch and dent items and wouldn't hesitate to do it again.  It looked as if they were only returned and had no visual defects.  If you don't like these choices go back after Christmas.  They always have a large stock with returned Christmas presents.||||reg||1
Z||000006||NEPTUNE||12-07-2001||04:14 PM||||If you order the Crutchfield catalog, there is a chart that will tell you what speakers will fit without modification. With slight mods, you can do a little better, but that is a great starting point. I haven't tried itb but they probably offer the same info on their website.  ||||reg||6
